## Account

The party record every commercial document links to (renamed from Customer to match the Revenue OS data architecture; the layer-matrix element is still Customer). Consumes base fields: `EmailField`, `PhoneNumberField` (E.164 string), `AddressField`, plus `domain`/`industry` strings and `owner = linksTo(Teammate)`.

Customer status is an event fact, not a stored flag: `firstPaidAt` is written once when the first payment lands (by the Record Payment command); `isCustomer` is `computeVia !!firstPaidAt`. Before that the account renders as Prospect.

```ts
import { Account } from '../account';
@field account = linksTo(Account);
```

Linked from Invoice, Order, and Subscription.

**Non-goals:** person/company split, multiple contacts per account (Contact card links here instead), pipeline status — those belong to the CRM records (Lead/Opportunity/Deal). Revenue rollups (totalRevenue, MRR) are NOT stored or computed here — they come from the AccountMetrics query block.
